==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Maeda Christmas''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Maeda Christmas DX''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Similarly to [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Maeda Keiji]], this unit can be used as either a tank against its trait or as a generalist midranger. Keiji Claus, however, despite not being as strong as Immortal Keiji, he still has some advantages in form of better range, pre-TF stats and activating his [[Strengthen]] ability earlier than pre-TF Maeda Keiji.

Unlike the original, however, this unit faces competition as a tank, mainly from a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]] and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]. This restricts its usage further, making Keiji Claus an unnecessary addition in most cases, although it can still help in wave centered stages (especially versus Red wave attackers like Two Can and Berserkory) or as a replacement for the two aforementioned units if they haven't been obtained yet.

Even then, as a generalist, when compared to Immortal Keiji, their health is lower and, despite having the same damage as them, due to their Strengthen activating at 40%, not 50%, the overall generalist value is still lower, despite being viable still.

==='''True Form'''===
This unit now targets [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and strengthens earlier, giving him a niche that not a lot of units have, being able to tank and dish out damage to Akus such as [[Aku Doge]], [[Sinner Snache]], and other peons. His Wave Immunity can be put to good use against the likes of Deathkory, Wicked Face and Diabrollow. He's not the best at dealing with [[Cerberus Kids]] due to their [[Freeze]] effect and also has no [[Shield Piercing|answer]] to shields, requiring support to efficiently defeat them.

==='''Talents'''===
Maeda Christmas DX benefits significantly from '''[[Immune to Surge]]''' and '''Strengthen'''. The former is mostly useful against Aku threats due to their tendency to abuse Surges, but he also has a niche as an anti-Surge midranger should the need arise. The latter works not too differently from how it did on on the original and further boosts his damage output. Likewise, '''HP Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' also serve him well if enough Catseyes have been invested. '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Freeze]]''' is situational due to the lack of viable matchups present for you to consider buying it.

==='''Orb'''===
Maeda Christmas DX can equip a Resistance Up Orb vs. either Red or Aku to further augment his abilities. Although one A-Rank Resist Freeze Orb can be combined with the respectively talent to grant him Freeze Immunity, it sees little application and is not recommended.

